When refine refuses
refine raises MeshRecognitionError, an input error with the problem locations, when:

nodes do not lie on one lattice;
cells fill no lattice square (a node at a third of a side, for example);
the 2:1 balance is broken (a square next to one more than one level coarser).

A mesh of rectangles or rotated cells has no lattice at all and raises an input error when it is read. On the command line the locations are written to &lt;output&gt;_recognition.gpkg. Duplicate nodes (two nodes at one point) are accepted: cells that touch only in such a point lose nothing, as flow goes through edges.
